<title>ITALY: TABLE-Italy markets see rates falling medium term.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Italy markets see rates falling medium term.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian money markets continue to expect a half basis point fall in interest rates over the next three months and see greater falls a year ahead, according to a study by the Igier research unit of the Bocconi University.</p>
<p>A study based on implicit overnight rates showed the implicit overnight rate at 6.83 percent one month on, unchanged from expectations last week. The actual overnight rate was 6.98 percent on Thursday, the day on which the study was based.</p>
<p>Three months out the implicit overnight rate is 6.57 percent unchanged from last week.</p>
<p>But a year ahead the implicit overnight rate is calculated at 5.93 percent, a shade under last week's 6.0 percent.</p>
<p>On a two-year horizon, the overnight rate is seen at 5.90 percent compared with a forecast of 6.07 percent last week.</p>
<p>Over the same time frame, the spread between the implied Italian overnight rate and that in Germany, considered a good indicator of confidence in Italy joining EMU, is at 145 basis points, down from 157 projected last week.</p>
